 and those are perhaps triggered  more in one person than in another  it's not so easy to analyze that ad  hocus  these are scientific questions that can  take a while to answer you can't cure or  understand an illness just like that in  one or two weeks it can take years some  people work their whole life to identify  the way an illness works  two years after inoculations began there  is still a lack of clinical studies on  the cause and treatment of side effects  we also need clinical algorithms so that  patients no longer remain in diagnostic  limbo  in advance  and we need treatment centers where they  know what to do  has at least brought her cardiological  problems under control  but her medical Odyssey continues both  neurologically and immunologically  after filming she was diagnosed with  damage to her immune system  which requires further treatment  Vera and Alexander who must first see if  his new medication helps him decide to  remain in contact they intend to compare  notes and support each other  [Music]  over 15 of the world's population live  with a disability a majority of them in  poor countries where Health Care is  lacking  these people were hit particularly hard  by the lockdowns with even the simplest  aspects of daily life posing big  problems  ew report Julius mogambua met up with a  blind man in uganda's capital Kampala  [Music]  got to messimi is passionate about music  and also about law  he wanted to study to become a lawyer  but then covid-19 hit  [Music]  he was due for an admissions test when  the university moved the applications  online  which left the blind man in the dark  establish the working rules because  everything was done online and for us we  were green about online I missed  pre-entries for mercury  as I had applied  um I couldn't come because by the time  we were supposed to come  they closed that transport and  schools were closed as well so I  couldn't be successful in law  to massimi is now studying to become a  teacher but he hasn't yet fully adapted  to e-learning  I had to look for someone to to help me  upload my examinations and sometimes  issues could happen and my exams could  not  upload truly load my performance if I'm  to compare my performance in year one  and here two here two is better because  yeah two we had no such issues we're  doing exams physically  at his university  signs with measures to prevent the  spread of covid-19 could be seen across  the campus  to massimi felt left out  it became an uncomfortable experience  I wasn't able to  identify those areas where water is to  wash my hands  unless I had maybe someone say come and  wash your hands that's when I could  realize but in most cases after entering  campus I got my guide like after three  weeks because you choose a guide for  yourself  and before  in those three weeks before getting a  guide even navigation the mobility  wasn't all that I could get lost  to different places  in the community tomasime faces related  challenges like accessing public  transportation  he says that this worsened during the  pandemic when the government shut it  down  there were no exceptions made  even for people with disabilities who  rely on support from others  we were restricted even when you're with  your guide you're moving on a border but  that they want you to be on separate  Buddha borders but at the end of it all  you get yourself lost  border borders uganda's motorbike taxis  were his Lifeline during the pandemic  which left him more isolated than usual  for the community members many people  have not understood us  they don't normally socialize with us  so it's very hard in the community about  three percent of uganda's 47 million  population are said to be visually  impaired they are part of a wider global  population of a billion people living  with some form of disability  research shows that during crises the  disabled often suffer most already when  you have a disability you have a budding  of dealing with 